        "exact_choice_count": null,
        "notes": "Scheduled intakes July each year. Application processing Applications are accepted: December 1st* to February 28th* March 1st* to April 15th* *or next business day Entrance requirements Applicants must meet the following entrance requirement: English language proficiency: Category 3 \u2013 English Studies 12 (50%) or equivalent Recommended for success To be successful in this program, students are recommended to possess the following: High school completion (or equivalent) Good computer proficiency, including Microsoft Word and Microsoft Excel Good communication skills and/or the desire to develop good communication skills An interest in exploring careers in the fields of architecture, construction, construction management, or engineering Access to a personal computer at home with a camera and microphone, and reliable internet service Access to a vehicle or public transportation, and a willingness to commute International applicants This program is not available to international students. View available programs . Apply to program Applications for this program are processed by the School of Construction and the Environment Industry Services department. Please contact Ann Martineau for more information on intakes and to receive a registration package. Go back Overview Next up Costs & Supplies",
